&\quad + (\text{\# that can do all three}) \\
&= 50 + 29 + 34 - 17 - 12 - 18 + 9 \\
&= 75
\end{align*}
However, we are not done yet. We need to account for the dogs that cannot perform any trick.
\begin{align*}
\text{Total number of dogs at the school} &= (\text{\# that can sit}) + (\text{\# that can stay}) + (\text{\# that can roll over}) \\
&\quad - (\text{\# that can sit and stay}) - (\text{\# that can stay and roll over}) - (\text{\# that can sit and roll over}) \\
&\quad + (\text{\# that can do all three}) + \text{(\# that cannot perform any trick)}\\
&= 75 + 9 = \boxed{84}
\end{align*}

Therefore, the total number of dogs at the Gooddog Obedience School is $\boxed{84}$.

