\end{align*}

Since $\sin^2{\frac{\theta}{2}} = (1 - \cos^2{\frac{\theta}{2}})$, we can write $$(\cos \theta)^2=\frac{(\sin^2{\frac{\theta}{2}})}{(\cos 2x)}$$ and substitute this value into our equation: 

\begin{align*}
3-4((\cos^2{\frac{\theta}{2}})^2)&=3-\frac{16}{360}V^2\\
