2. In this case, we have n = 15 (total number of students) and k = 13 (number of students to be selected).
3. Plug in the values: C(15, 13) = \frac{15!}{13!(15-13)!}
4. Simplify the expression by canceling out the common factors: C(15, 13) = \frac{15!}{13!2!}
