The sum of the interior angles of a polygon can be found using the formula $180(n-2)$, where n is the number of sides of the polygon.

For an octagon, which has 8 sides, we can plug in n=8 into the formula:

$$180(8-2) = 180 \cdot 6 = 1080$$

The sum of the interior angles of a regular octagon is therefore $1080$ degrees. Since all interior angles are congruent, each angle has measure $\frac{1080}{8}$.

\boxed{\begin{equation*}
\frac{1080}{8} = \boxed{135}
\end{equation*}}

