Let's solve this system of equations using substitution or elimination.
If we use substitution, we can start by expressing $c$ in terms of $a$ and $b$ from one of the equations. For example, using the equation $ab=48$, we have 
\begin{align*}
    bc &= 48 \\
    c &= \frac{1}{2} ab
\end{align*}
Substituting this into our original expression for $(abc)^2 =  (4\sqrt{3})(49)(50)$, we get
\begin{align*}
   (abc)^2 &= (4\sqrt{3})^2 \cdot 49 \cdot 50 \\
           &= 48 \cdot 2560 \\
           &= 124,800
\end{align*}
Therefore, 
\begin{align*}
    (abc) &= \frac{124,800}{49} = 2646.931 \approx 2646 
\end{align*}
and $c$ is approximately equal to 
\begin{align*}
    c &= \frac{1}{2} ab = \frac{1/2}(2\cdot 646) = 653 \\
\end{align*}
So the volume of the right rectangular prism is 
\begin{align*}
   V &= a(ab)(c) \\
    &= (646)\cdot(4)(653) \\
    &= 1,049,928 \\
\end{align*}
which is approximately equal to 1,010,000.

