$$
\frac{-1-5i}{13}
$$

Since $i$ appears in both the numerator and denominator, we can simplify by dividing both by 1, which does not change the value of the fraction:
$$
\begin{aligned}
\frac{-1-5i}{13} &= \frac{(-1-5i)}{13} \\
&= -\frac{1+5i}{13}
\end{aligned}
$$

