1. The first step is to express the product of square roots as a single square root of the product of the numbers inside the individual square roots. This means that $\sqrt{75x} \cdot \sqrt{2x} \cdot \sqrt{14x}$ can be rewritten as $\sqrt{75x \cdot 2x \cdot 14x}$.

\begin{align*}
& \sqrt{75x} \cdot \sqrt{2x} \cdot \sqrt{14x}\\
= & \sqrt{(75x)(2x)(14x)}\\
= & \sqrt{2100x^3}
\end{align*}

2. The next step is to simplify the expression under the square root by finding the prime factorization of 2100. 

\begin{align*}
& \sqrt{2100x^3}\\
= & \sqrt{(4)(525)x^3} \\
= & \sqrt{(2)^2(5^2)(21)(5x^3)}\\
= & (2)(5x)\sqrt{(21)(5x)}
\end{align*}

3. We can simplify the expression under the square root further by combining the terms with $x$ and the constants.

\begin{align*}
& \sqrt{2100x^3}\\
= & (2)(5x)\sqrt{(21)(5x)}\\
= & 10x\sqrt{105x}
\end{align*}

The final answer is: $\boxed{10x\sqrt{105x}}$

